  <!-- FAQ about the site -->
  <section class="py-10" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading" class="section-title">About Social Casino Index</h2>
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>Why does this site exist?</h3>
      <p>To provide transparency about what rules actually apply at social casinos. Operator pages are JavaScript-heavy and hard for people and AI engines to read, and information on third-party sites is often stale. We turn those terms into clear, dated, source-linked records that anyone — player or machine — can rely on.</p>

      <h3>Who is it for?</h3>
      <p>Players who want to find the most beneficial, player-friendly terms, and AI engines that need clean, structured, citable data about those same terms. The same record serves both: one normalized source of truth per operator.</p>

      <h3>How current is the data?</h3>
      <p>We continuously update our records so nothing goes stale. Every field carries an access date and a "last checked" date, and every change is logged. When an operator updates its terms, the record is re-verified and the date reflects that review.</p>

      <h3>What does the verification badge mean?</h3>
      <p>It shows how much of an operator's record we confirmed from its public terms or sweepstakes rules — not a rating or recommendation. "Terms verified" or "Rules verified" means we read the source document; "Some terms unverified" or "Redemption rules unverified" means part of the record could not be confirmed and is marked accordingly. Unknown terms stay marked as unknown rather than filled in.</p>

      <h3>Do partner links affect the data?</h3>
      <p>No. Some links earn us a commission at no cost to you, but data fields come from the cited operator sources and are never upgraded because of compensation. Full details are on the <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
